# The pinned wire-harness release this checkout consumes (#246).
#
# The harness — the headless build-5875 wire client and the LyraCore orchestrators around it — used
# to be `tools/wire-client/` in this workspace. It is its own repository now,
# LyraCoreProject/wire-harness, because it is a SERVER-AGNOSTIC protocol tool: nothing in it depends
# on a LyraCore crate, and a workspace membership was the coupling that made "would this run against
# any other 5875 core?" unanswerable.
#
# ONE line: `<tag> <full commit sha>`, and BOTH halves are load-bearing.
#   * the TAG is what `scripts/wire-harness.sh` checks out — a release, not a branch. There is
#     deliberately no way to say "main" here.
#   * the SHA is what it then VERIFIES the checkout resolved to. A git tag is a mutable ref; a
#     re-pointed tag would otherwise change what this checkout builds without changing this file,
#     which is the one thing a pin exists to prevent.
#
# To bump: put the new tag + the commit it resolves to on the line below and commit it. See
# `docs/development-cli.md` ("dev smoke") first — a bump is a behaviour change to every live wire
# test.
